  and also want to  reorient you to the this map that we  have here of the weight loss  um pointing out specifically when weight  loss occurs which is on day six and when  we start seeing weight gain which is on  day nine and so when we're seeing the  accumulation of these plural macrophages  within the lung is when we're actually  seeing the animals starting to regain  weight which would suggest that these  pleural macrophages are involved more in  a in the resolution of the Z in the in  the resolution of disease  we also asked what these pkh positive  lung cells were are they alveolar  macrophages are they interstitial  macrophages and we found that these pkh  positive cells are actually cd11 B  positive indicating that they are  interstitial macrophages they're not  alveolar macrophages they don't have um  Sig like f  we also asked where are these pkh  positive lung cells so here we have some  microscopy images of the lungs  in red we have  um our pkh stained macrophages and in  blue we have dappy which is staining all  the cells  the top panel shows our PBS animals and  so we don't see any red because the  there are no macrophages going into the  the lung and on the bottom panel we have  our collo9 infected animals and you see  the accumulation of these plural  macrophages in the lung  um near to the mesothelia layer so the  little dotted white line there is the  mesothelial layer  so pleural macrophages accumulate in the  lung near the mesothelium  so we then ask do pleural macrophages  influenza outcomes so it's great that  they're going into the lung but are they  even doing anything are they of  are they even important  so  to test this we  did an intra-pural  um injection of quadrinate liposomes so  what this is is that quadronate  basically is a poison and the liposome  will direct this poison specifically to  phagocytic cells  um in the pleural cavity and so when you  inject these quadrinate ribosomes the  pleural macrophages in the pleural  cavity will p